==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{enPR|spô}}, {{IPA|/spɔː/|lang=en}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{enPR|spôr}}, {{IPA|/spɔɹ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|rhotic|horse-hoarse}} {{enPR|spōr}}, {{IPA|/spo(ː)ɹ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|nonrhotic|horse-hoarse}} {{IPA|/spoə/|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|spoor}} {{qualifier|accents with the {{w|pour–poor merger}}}}
* {{rhymes|ɔː(ɹ)|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From Modern Latin {{m|la|spora}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|σπορά||seed, a sowing}}, related to {{m|grc|σπόρος||sowing}} and {{m|grc|σπείρω||to sow}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*sper-||to strew}} (compare English {{m|en|spread}}).

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
{{wikipedia}}

# A [[reproductive]] particle, usually a single [[cell]], released by a [[fungus]], [[alga]], or [[plant]] that may [[germinate]] into another.
# A [[thick]] [[resistant]] particle produced by a [[bacterium]] or [[protist]] to survive in [[harsh]] or [[unfavorable]] conditions.

